# The README and the CI workflow both build the binary into the repository
# root, so it lands here on any ordinary day of work.
/git-ticket

# goreleaser writes its archives, checksums and metadata here. Ignoring it is
# not tidiness: `go build` records whether the tree was modified, and it counts
# an untracked file as a modification, so an unignored dist/ would stamp
# `modified: true` into every binary a release published. --version reports that
# field, and plan 12.1 has it read from the build rather than from an ldflag,
# so the provenance is only honest while this line is here.
/dist/
